{"availability":"available","full":"Timmoth/AsyncMonolith","name":"AsyncMonolith","description":"Facilitates simple durable and asynchronous messaging in dotnet apps.","category":"Other","language":"C#","stars":93,"forks":7,"created":"2024-06-03T18:07:00Z","updated":"2026-01-28T23:33:42Z","license":"Apache-2.0","branch":"main","homepage":"","topics":["async","csharp","dotnet","efcore","messaging","outbox","scheduler","transactional"],"demo":"https://timmoth.github.io/AsyncMonolith/demo","color":"#25392f","ink":"#d1e5c5","lastCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:57.913Z","lastAttemptAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:57.913Z","lastAvailableAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:57.913Z","metrics":[{"at":"2026-10-08T04:51:57.913Z","stars":93,"forks":7}],"technologies":[],"overview":{"kind":"readme","version":1,"paragraphs":["AsyncMonolith is a lightweight library that facilitates simple, durable and asynchronous messaging in dotnet apps.","Despite its name, AsyncMonolith can be used within a microservices architecture. The only requirement is that the producers and consumers share the same database i.e messaging within a single project. However, it is not suitable for passing messages between different projects in a microservices architecture, as microservices should not share the same database."],"features":["Speed up your API by offloading tasks to a background worker.","Distribute workload amongst multiple app instances.","Execute tasks at specific times or after a delay.","Execute tasks at regular intervals.","Simplify complex processes by building out an event-driven architecture."],"sourceUrl":"https://github.com/Timmoth/AsyncMonolith/blob/main/README.md","fingerprint":"4426c5aaada848398136e1f96bd34d7fccf427527b6f50161785b27f3acb401c","extractedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:58.004Z"},"overviewCheckedAt":"2026-10-08T04:51:58.004Z","projectInsights":{"version":1,"whatItDoes":{"text":"AsyncMonolith is a lightweight library that facilitates simple, durable and asynchronous messaging in dotnet apps.","sourceUrl"